{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1498600-gauru-form-too-strong","id":1498600,"title":"Gauru form too strong?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-12-01T21:04:39-08:00","id":1498600,"title":"Gauru form too strong?","content":"I'm struggling to find some drawback that helps balance the massive buffs Gauru form gives to a werewolf. It lasts forever (even the lowest durations last longer than any combat I've ever run in my 7+ years of running Chronicles of Darkness), it doesn't cost anything, and it makes the character much more powerful and nearly unkillable. I don't see why you wouldn't use it in every combat you go into. Maybe if it only lasted a turn or two, or you could only use it once per game day, or it cost willpower every turn, or something, but as it is it just rubs me the wrong way. Has anyone else found this? Has anyone come up with good house rules that help make gauru form a bit less of an auto use all the time ability? I'm guessing there hasn't been any official errata on gauru form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-01T21:54:34-08:00","id":1498606,"title":"","content":"Don\u2019t remember the exact rules ATM, but Gauru also throws you into rage, during which you break everything and everyone, including anything you like/adore/love. And you can be led into a trap by clever and resourceful hunters, in which you will not be happy when you finally get a hold of yourself. So it\u2019s not always the best option to run with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-02T00:51:18-08:00","id":1498609,"title":"","content":"The Gauru Rage, the risk for Death Rage, as well as the once per scene limit for safe usage are the main limits.<br /> <br /> On top of that, you could always use antagonists that have tactics for dealing with Gauru (stalling and/or keeping out of reach works great for letting Gauru lapse or go into uncontrolled rage where the werewolf can be redirected to others).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-02T06:14:09-08:00","id":1498618,"title":"","content":"Gauru has plenty of drawbacks, you can only use it once per scene and up to your hishu form stamina plus primal urge (which means that if you take it when you are out of reach you are going to waste it), for most characters this is 4 or 5 turns, and if you do anything else but attacking something or someone you have to roll and if you fail then it's kuruth time which is a massive problem, especially if you are near people, also while it does make werewolves very powerful, it has diminishing returns in the long run since you are going to face spirits that are far more powerful than you, werewolves who default to gauru to rip and tear don't live long, it is something that must be used when it's the killing time not before.<br /> <br /> It is also worth mentioning that gauru doesn't increase your defense that much and short of a few gifts, werewolves don't have many long range options, this means that possessed hosts with silver bullets can and will end you before you can reach them if you are not careful, hunters who know about uratha in particular will purposefuly bait werewolves to leave them defenseless, gauru is a massive advantage for werewolves but it doesn't make them unkillable.<br /> <br /> There is also the fact that CofD isn't the world of darkness, werewolves going on rampages and stacking bodies left and right will raise questions, gauru can easily lead to kuruth and if you let your players get away with butchering a shopping mall worth of people because they carelessly took gauru to fight that rank 2 flunkie then you are doing it wrong, the consequences of an hunt can be dire and long lasting and your players should always keep that in mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-03T12:09:12-08:00","id":1498694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1498600-gauru-form-too-strong#post1498600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm struggling to find some drawback that helps balance the massive buffs Gauru form gives to a werewolf. It lasts forever (even the lowest durations last longer than any combat I've ever run in my 7+ years of running Chronicles of Darkness), it doesn't cost anything, and it makes the character much more powerful and nearly unkillable. I don't see why you wouldn't use it in every combat you go into. Maybe if it only lasted a turn or two, or you could only use it once per game day, or it cost willpower every turn, or something, but as it is it just rubs me the wrong way. Has anyone else found this? Has anyone come up with good house rules that help make gauru form a bit less of an auto use all the time ability? I'm guessing there hasn't been any official errata on gauru form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why wouldn't you use it in every combat? What, are you always trying to kill anyone and everyone who feels like they have to bodily stand against you?<br /> <br /> EDIT: I really need to do that combat thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 12-03-2022, 11:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-03T13:16:35-08:00","id":1498699,"title":"","content":"Also:<br /> <br /> &quot;Too strong&quot; is a comparative construction. Too strong for what? Compared to what? In what context? What is the baseline that you want Gauru to be lined up against to confirm that appropriateness of its levels of strength?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-03T18:29:02-08:00","id":1498717,"title":"","content":"No, it's not &quot;too strong&quot;.<br /> <br /> A werewolf chronicle likely provides an array of adversaries for the werewolves which is composed, at least in part, of incredibly powerful entities. <br /> Take a peek in the Prey chapter and have a good read of the Horrors and Wonders chapter in the Chronicles of Darkness book. <br /> <br /> <i>That's </i>what werewolves were designed to contend with, and that's why the nerf hammer needs to stay the fuck away from Gauru form. <br /> <br /> Don't be afraid of moments where the PCs get to demonstrate just how powerful and terrifying they can be when compared with regular mortals or lesser adversaries. There's plenty of powerful stuff that can threaten a pack.<br /> <br /> Also, it's the Chronicles of Darkness. It's okay to be &quot;too strong&quot; every now and again. Being &quot;too strong&quot; can be a source of horror for the characters and players as well as the storyteller characters. <br /> A werewolf entering Gauru at an inopportune moment and falling into Kuruth can result in a lot of regret for the werewolf when she comes out of it and looks at the corpse of a loved one or a bystander. <br /> <br /> You play <i>monsters </i>here.<br /> Monsters <i>should </i>be scary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1807-serpent-axis","name":"Serpent Axis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1807_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-04T23:12:47-08:00","id":1498819,"title":"","content":"Another point in relation to what I said earlier: it's also ok to let the players be powerful every now and again, and not always with obligatory horror or fallout. <br /> <br /> In the Chronicles of Darkness, we get to play monsters and powerful characters. Those monsters have <i>a lot</i> of problems they contend with, they have enemies - powerful enemies - and face dangers that most action heroes would soil themselves over. <br /> But power is part of the appeal here.<br /> <br /> You didn't just choose to play a werewolf because you thought that's how you'll get the biggest boot on your neck all game. You wanted to play werewolf because you also want, every now and again, to pin a motherfucker to the wall and give him a growl full of fangs and fur that makes the sorry bastard wet himself. <br /> <br /> They're powerful? <i>Let them</i>. <br /> Let them be powerful.<br /> <br /> Let the vampire player get ambushed by an entire street gang and their mother, only for the same player to then make the leader her bitch just by looking into his eyes. <br /> <br /> Let the demon player dispatch an entire SWAT team like something out of Equilibrium or the Matrix.<br /> <br /> Let them be powerful and give them their moments of unbridled, supernatural power. <br /> It's part of the appeal of the game, part of the reason they're playing Werewolf and not Call of Cthulhu. It's their brand of horror, where sometimes the source of the horror <i>is the players themselves</i>. <br /> <br /> Trust me, there's enough challenges and powerful enemies in any CofD chronicle to go around. In my opinion, it's like a rollercoaster - and every rollercoaster should have highs as well as lows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1807-serpent-axis","name":"Serpent Axis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1807_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-05T06:12:37-08:00","id":1498843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Serpent Axis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1498600-gauru-form-too-strong?p=1498819#post1498819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another point in relation to what I said earlier: it's also ok to let the players be powerful every now and again, and not always with obligatory horror or fallout.<br /> <br /> In the Chronicles of Darkness, we get to play monsters and powerful characters. Those monsters have <i>a lot</i> of problems they contend with, they have enemies - powerful enemies - and face dangers that most action heroes would soil themselves over.<br /> But power is part of the appeal here.<br /> <br /> You didn't just choose to play a werewolf because you thought that's how you'll get the biggest boot on your neck all game. You wanted to play werewolf because you also want, every now and again, to pin a motherfucker to the wall and give him a growl full of fangs and fur that makes the sorry bastard wet himself.<br /> <br /> They're powerful? <i>Let them</i>.<br /> Let them be powerful.<br /> <br /> Let the vampire player get ambushed by an entire street gang and their mother, only for the same player to then make the leader her bitch just by looking into his eyes.<br /> <br /> Let the demon player dispatch an entire SWAT team like something out of Equilibrium or the Matrix.<br /> <br /> Let them be powerful and give them their moments of unbridled, supernatural power.<br /> It's part of the appeal of the game, part of the reason they're playing Werewolf and not Call of Cthulhu. It's their brand of horror, where sometimes the source of the horror <i>is the players themselves</i>.<br /> <br /> Trust me, there's enough challenges and powerful enemies in any CofD chronicle to go around. In my opinion, it's like a rollercoaster - and every rollercoaster should have highs as well as lows.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I couldn't agree more, I will also add that Werewolf is also a game about feeling powerful, you are a monster designed to hunt and kill gods, you are supposed to be the one with the biggest dick in the room, the problems and the horror of the game are in the aftermath because realistically, there aren't that many occasions where you will be seriously threatened, I mean yes, rank 5 spirits will wipe the floor with the pack if you are not careful but most of the time, you will be dealing with things far more manageable.<br /> <br /> Human hunters will be a joke for the most part (yeah, silver bullets are much more common in real life and can be bought online but you are not supposed to throw silver at your players like candy anyway) and spirits will go down similarly easy if you do your research, which is actually what most of the game will be about, you are an hunter, you will spend most of your time investigating events that might or might not involve spirits, you will search for clues, look at crime scenes and do honest to god detective work most of the time then, after you think you will have gathered enough clues, you will hit the books (methaporical or literal ones) and start researching about that one particular spirit that is fucking up your territory, you will look for it's weaknesses, it's strengths and whether or not it has allies, you will go on until you literally know life, death and miracles about your fucking prey, then, at that point, you start making a plan, you isolate your prey, cut it off from it's support network, remove it's ability to fight back, leave it at it's most vulnerable, you will chase and harry it until it can no longer stand up, until that one moment it will know how incredibly fucked it truly is, then you go gauru and it is over in seconds.<br /> <br /> As you can see, gauru will only come up at the end and it won't last more than a couple of turns at most which is by design, werewolf is a lot more than go gauru and rip and tear, you are the ultimate predator and should act like one, the horror comes when you fuck up the hunting part of the game and end up ripping apart a young girl you thought it was an host and have to watch her while she chokes on her own blood and with her guts hanging out because you were too much of an incompetent fuck to properly identify your prey or when you lose control during an hunt and the world goes black only to wake up and find out that you killed a few wolf blooded members of your pack, gauru will not save you from this stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-19T22:33:05-08:00","id":1500813,"title":"","content":"Even in gauru form being outnumbered or up against heavy weapons is a tricky prospect. The system is very hard on the outnumbered character; multiple gunmen focusing fire on the same target can overwhelm the gauru form's healing surprisingly fast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-20T00:59:41-08:00","id":1500821,"title":"","content":"It is worth putting an asterisk on that because &quot;nameless mook brigade&quot; vs. &quot;squad of experienced monster-hunters&quot; is a huge difference when it comes to overwhelming Gauru with numbers. Harshest Lunacy, Primal Fear, and full defense against firearms makes Gauru fairly resistant to trying to wear down with a horde of mooks: a lot of them are going to lose their nerve and run, and forcing them into Down &amp; Dirty roll offs helps counter the system's bias towards numerical superiority. A squad of hunters that are going to have the stats to resist Lunacy, not be too hindered by the increased defense and small penalty to their actions, and aren't stuck dealing with Down &amp; Dirty are going to easily win out over Gauru form's regeneration and raw stat boosts.<br /> <br /> The difficult part about any idea of addressing &quot;too strong&quot; is that this is a narrative differentiation rather than a mechanical one. The hunters don't need radically better stats than the mooks, just the narrative weight of being serious foes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-20T08:02:56-08:00","id":1500839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1498600-gauru-form-too-strong?p=1500821#post1500821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The difficult part about any idea of addressing &quot;too strong&quot; is that this is a narrative differentiation rather than a mechanical one. The hunters don't need radically better stats than the mooks, just the narrative weight of being serious foes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, that about covers it pretty well. It's actually in a pretty good place, I think - a SWAT team has a reasonable chance of coming out on top, or at least with a few survivors, and the National Guard can probably put you down in a pinch, but Gauru form is absolutely no joke against anyone not very heavily armed or ready for werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-30T02:23:56-08:00","id":1501676,"title":"","content":"How does it lasts forever, if your typical werewolf-newbie with Stamina 2-3 aand PU 1 can keep ot only at 3-4 turns. <br /> Anyway, pretty mich every splat has it's own broken tricks. Vampires have barely unlimited Bloodbounds, Changellings can run away into the Hedge., etc. etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T09:44:29-08:00","id":1502213,"title":"","content":"I think the Garou warform is one of the most innovative features in roleplaying and has sparked debate since the game was released. Oceans of ink have been used on this topic. <br /> <br /> Yes, the Garou form is extremely powerful, how is it a curse? The threat of Kuruth takes away agency from the player. You are basically giving the car keys to a raging monster. We can explore ideas such as causing it aggravated damage, evading Kuruth, the consequences of Kuruth, and how it can violate the Oath of the Moon.<br /> <br /> Causing Damage.<br /> <br /> There are numerous cases of how heavy weapons can cause enough damage to &quot;roll over&quot; and fill the track with aggravated damage. Arm 12 humans (cultists...claimed...hunters...ghouls...etc) with automatic rifles and you can probably destroy an entire pack in Kuruth in 1 roll. Look at the devourer hound in the prey section and one can challenge an Uratha, while 3 or 4 can probably destroy the war form in a few short rounds. A level 2 spirit can pump up his stats to a degree that 3 of them can roll over lethal to aggravated quite quickly. <br /> <br /> This is before looking at vulnerabilities like silver. I reckon $20.00 can buy on ounce of silver shot to put in a shotgun. Arm 10 hunters (ghouls, cultists...) and you have a major issue to face. Remember also that uratha can cause aggravated damage by eating essence so remember that when facing the Predator Kings.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T09:58:44-08:00","id":1502214,"title":"","content":"Evading Kuruth<br /> <br /> if you can't cause damage, just run away until the timer ends. Various powers include turning to mist, amplifying speed, running up a wall, melting into the earth, flying away, dematerializing, etc. I would imagine a spirit in twilight can just watch and materialize after the carnage. Alternatively, you send a wave of expendable flunkies on a suicide mission to provoke Kuruth (cultists, claimed, ghouls, followers...) and then move in after the Kuruth ends<br /> <br /> Consequences<br /> <br /> If a packmate succumbs to Kuruth, does the pack follow him ( potentially dooming the pack) or restrain him? Imagine an Uratha trying to fight the war form without succumbing, that would be a scary battle. I think about the final episode of Witcher Blood oath which shows a pack dealing with a pack member who fell into rage.<br /> <br /> Oath of the Moon<br /> <br /> Finally, Kuruth can lead to violations such as killing other Uratha, eating human flesh, or exposing the People to humans. One of the hunting grounds in the main book is Tokyo. Can an Uratha go into Kuruth in Tokyo and not be noticed? Doing a sloppy job of keeping the herd ignorant can expose Uratha to hunters not only in your region, but globally with the advent of global media.<br /> <br /> Much more can be explored on this topic. This is just a brief thesis","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T10:11:32-08:00","id":1502215,"title":"","content":"Really, the big drawback of Garau is, as others have touched upon, it's complete lack of access to non-lethal options. If you need someone alive for some reason you're going to stick to one of the other forms, particularly Hishu and Dalu for tool access (rope, your choice of less lethal weapon, setting up some kind of trap...). Garau's purpose is to spread fear and death, it's either the finale of a hunt or a last ditch desperate attempt to scars others before taking another form and escape (and if you're using it for that something's go r horribly wrong).<br /> <br /> Note that 1e Garau was considered underpowered thanks to the Rage, which is why 2e upped it to ten seconds of murder (or at the absolute peak about a minute, but who actually hits Power Stat 10?). It's very intentionally not Crinos, and a smart werewolf defaults to Dalu or Urshal for most combat, but it's a useful tool for when you need to make the kill right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-14T17:07:38-08:00","id":1503084,"title":"","content":"I've been a fan of playing werewolves since the Apocalypse; they're supposed to be powerful, but, it's all how you play them. <br /> <br /> A lot of players I've known liked to play games in which they were powerful. In <i>Dark Sun</i>, one player loved to be physical and play Fighters and Gladiators, until he learned what Templars could do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-30T23:57:53-07:00","id":1507024,"title":"","content":"I think my biggest problem with Gauru form is the healing. All a character has to do is shift up, clear all lethal damage (bashing is already something they can clear super fast), then shift back down. It's impossible to keep damage on a werewolf unless it's aggravated. It creates the superman problem. Superman is impervious to all damage, so attacking him is pointless, unless you use the mcguffin (kryptonite/silver/whatever) which can put him down almost instantly. So enemies are either pointless (no silver) or super deadly (with silver), there is no middle ground. Werewolves in gauru form destroying everything around them? Actually they only have to attack an enemy, and only one that's still active. They never attack friends or innocents, and don't have to kill the enemy. If it acted more like a vampire's frenzy then maybe it would be ok. 3-5 round being nothing? What game are you playing? I don't think I've ever had a combat go past 3-4 rounds. This isn't D&amp;D, combat in CoD is fast. Simply evading and defending against a werewolf in gauru form for 5+ rounds is asking a hell of a lot, especially when you take some of the other bs werewolf combat gifts into account, and it makes for a long and boring combat if the enemy just dodges every round. Maybe if the healing thing was toned down, or it cost essense every round the werewolf remained in gauru form, or a werewolf in gauru form had to all-out attack every round (no defense), or the duration was much lower, or it could only be used once per chapter and not per scene, or the gauru had to attack uncontrollably rather than being able to focus on only enemies, any of these things would make it so much more balanced. And I'm talking about balanced as in against the game in general and what other splats can do. I know CoD plays it loose when it comes to game balance, but there are some things that are just unfairly strong and/or completely unbalanced. There's a difference between being strong and being broken, and garu form is leaning pretty heavy on the later. I guess when it comes to dealing with werewolves I'll just have to give everyone kryptonite, sorry I mean silver weapons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-31T03:30:03-07:00","id":1507045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1498600-gauru-form-too-strong?p=1507024#post1507024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So enemies are either pointless (no silver) or super deadly (with silver), there is no middle ground.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having played a fair bit of Forsaken 2e this was not my experience.<br /> <br /> Let's take for example the time our pack fought a pack of Pure. We caused the Pure pack to all death rage near the start of the combat (by murdering their totem). They all took Gauru form, and we mostly stayed in Dalu and Urshul form. We managed to wipe out the Pure pack without using any silver. How? By focusing on one enemy at a time. We used our gifts, positioning, and misdirection to make sure that most of the Pure were chasing after shadows and not able to bring their strength to bear. We then focused down one enemy before moving on to the next. A Gauru form Werewolf only heals their health track in lethal each turn - for most Werewolves this is going to be about 11 damage. Dealing 11 damage across 2-3 attacks in a turn is not very difficult. One thing we found useful was that you can make characters with lethal damage attack first in the round to fill up those 11 boxes. Any characters dealing bashing damage can then attack later in the same round and it will count as agg regardless. It took us about 2 rounds to take down each of the Pure using these tactics.<br /> <br /> Another tactic that was used against us by the ST on several occasions was grappling. A character who is built for grappling can get some very high dice pools, even compared to a Gauru. On more than one occasion when we took Gauru form or fell to kuruth, we ended up in a grapple which we lost, and the ST used the &quot;Restrain&quot; manoeuvre. As long as an enemy is able to maintain the grapple, this pretty much takes a Gauru out of the fight.<br /> <br /> Gauru are not invincible, and a well prepared enemy can deal with one pretty quickly. One of our pack nearly died in one of the first sessions because they got cocky about Gauru form and rounded a corner into 4 guys with automatic weapons. Smart Werewolf players will use all the tools at their disposal to separate, harry, and corner the prey. When they take Gauru form to make the kill the outcome should already be decided.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-31T13:22:41-07:00","id":1507072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1498600-gauru-form-too-strong?p=1507024#post1507024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolves in gauru form destroying everything around them? Actually they only have to attack an enemy, and only one that's still active. They never attack friends or innocents, and don't have to kill the enemy.</div> </div> </div> </div>You need to re-read Rage on Page 97. They must attack an enemy or move toward attacking an enemy, even if that means attacking a downed enemy. If there are no enemies remaining they will lash out and attack whomever is within reach. Attempting to do anything else requires a roll.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Simply evading and defending against a werewolf in gauru form for 5+ rounds is asking a hell of a lot, especially when you take some of the other bs werewolf combat gifts into account, </div> </div> </div>Remember, attempting to do anything other than smash while in Gauru requires a roll or fall into Kuruth, as per Rage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and it makes for a long and boring combat if the enemy just dodges every round. </div> </div> </div>So don't have the foe do that. Look at the Evasion gift Hit and Run. Consider any number of possible influences that could prevent attacks. Give out tilts and conditions. Heck, send in fodder first then when the pack has shifted out of Gauru form come in and wreck face.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe if the healing thing was toned down, or it cost essense every round the werewolf remained in gauru form, or a werewolf in gauru form had to all-out attack every round (no defense), or the duration was much lower, or it could only be used once per chapter and not per scene, or the gauru had to attack uncontrollably rather than being able to focus on only enemies, any of these things would make it so much more balanced. </div> </div> </div>Gauru form isn't meant to be &quot;balanced&quot; compared to the other forms, it's a wrecking ball. It does one thing, and it does it very, very well. That's okay. Hit it sideways. Work around it. Flex as a storyteller.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And I'm talking about balanced as in against the game in general and what other splats can do. </div> </div> </div>Have you read the other splats? A mage has a thousand and one options for dealing with a Gauru werewolf. A demon can put it to sleep with no roll, so long as they're able to touch it with a brawl attack, the attack doesn't even need to do damage. A deviant can regenerate from ashes and deal aggravated damage all day every day. A Changeling can go toe to toe with a Gauru werewolf and match or exceed it's dicepool and dish out aggravated damage with every attack. ... I'm not quite sure what a sin eater can do, I don't want to spend time flipping through the book 15 times, but something cool and ghostly I would hope.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-31T14:46:19-07:00","id":1507081,"title":"","content":"The Superman thing also feels like an example that helps prove the opposite point.<br /> <br /> Superman goes up against foes that don't have Kryptonite all the time, and they're serious opposition. His iconic foil is Lex Luther who doesn't have any superpowers and has taken on Kal more than once without having to resort to Kryptonite. While you can debate if Lex is smarter or not (objective measures are hard and they demonstrate intelligence in vastly different ways), Lex is certainly far more ruthless and cunning. He knows how to us his enemies' morals, emotional vulnerabilities, and similar points of attack to maximum effect and will absolutely do so.<br /> <br /> Superman also has plenty of foes that are just up to fighting him. Physical powerhouses on his level, fighters that can make up the ground by exploiting his other big weakness (no innate defenses against magic), foes that you can't beat just by being stronger than them (Parasite being a stereotypical example as the more powerful the hero, the more they just feed him and it's actually better to let the more 'normal' heroes take him down).<br /> <br /> Superman writers have come up with a laundry list of ways to make conflicts interesting despite how ridiculously powerful the big blue boy scout is. Forsaken has left in lots of ways to deal with Gauru form besides silver. As well covered above on of the big things is to be Luthor: fight smarter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-31T18:23:08-07:00","id":1507090,"title":"","content":"CofD2e is also honestly a rather high powered game by WoD standards. Even ignoring outliers like Mage and Mummy supernatural powers tend to spike pretty high, and both weapons and damage downgrading tend to be more significant than they were previously. A kindred built for combat focused on the physical disciplines can probably match or exceed a Garau Uratha's dice pools in anything but defence Vs firearms, and has the advantage of a lot.<br /> <br /> Its also not going to be too hard to deal aggravated damage if you can focus reliable sources of Lethal at a target. IIRC Uratha don't get to downgrade weapon damage (I briefly checked the parts of the book I could think of, but it's late so I might have missed something) and most will likely have 10-11 Health in Garau form, so a dozen trained marksmen could down one in 2-4 rounds if they resisted Lunacy. Werewolves' intended major enemies (spirits, hosts, claimed, other werewolves, human-derived supernaturals) all have more reliable ways of either dealing damage or just shutting down the rage monster entirely.<br /> <br /> When you have the advantage nothing beats Garau when going in for the kill. <i>That's the point</i>. I also suppose that with a clever player or unimaginative ST you could have the advantage pretty often. But it's massive advantages are outweighed by basically cutting off basic tactics without making a roll, and if you can't reliably make that roll than relying on Garau means you're easy to lure into a trap.<br /> <br /> <br /> But really, all I'm imagining now is what happens if a Uratha enters Garau form, then a vampire with dominate uses their powers, points at their friend, and says something along the lines of 'kill them'. Sure, it's an issue in any form, but in Garau you're not allowed to weasel your way around the 'it'll be easier to kill them if I X first' line of logic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-31T21:24:46-07:00","id":1507096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1498600-gauru-form-too-strong?p=1507090#post1507090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC Uratha don't get to downgrade weapon damage (I briefly checked the parts of the book I could think of, but it's late so I might have missed something) and most will likely have 10-11 Health in Garau form, so a dozen trained marksmen could down one in 2-4 rounds if they resisted Lunacy.</div> </div> </div> </div>They've got the same caveat vampires get that things which would deal aggravated damage to humans that aren't supernatural powers (e.g. massive bodily devastation) deal lethal instead, per the section on Regeneration, and Fortified Form beyond the basic level can give a form a ballistic Armor rating, but other than that, yeah, nothing intrinsic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-01T13:37:31-07:00","id":1507116,"title":"","content":"While I wrote the <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501082-let-s-talk-about-combat-in-chronicles-of-darkness\">combat essay</a> because I've seen way too many threads that misunderstand combat in Chronicles to put up with it anymore, it is specifically the way some Forsaken fans just don't get it that drove me over the edge, and I think I'm actually grateful for the good excuse to thoroughly deconstruct what I commonly see wrong when it comes up.<br /> <br /> I do want that combat thread to be in the back of people's minds for this, but since it's a lot, I want to iterate two particular points here just for ground:<br /> <br /> 1) No one gets into a fight just to have a fight, and the majority of the time, they don't want it to be a fight, so much as an overwhelming steamrolling action that would never switch into the system, or otherwise getting the fuck out alive.<br /> 2) All of the above then becomes a matter of resource management, on all levels, and weighing the gamble of any and all expenditures against the net success.<br /> <br /> So with that said.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowdragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1498600-gauru-form-too-strong?p=1507024#post1507024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think my biggest problem with Gauru form is the healing. All a character has to do is shift up, clear all lethal damage (bashing is already something they can clear super fast), then shift back down.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gauru is the biggest reason things are perpetually misunderstood here in Forsakenland, and I keep seeing the argument about healing in particular, so let's break this down.<br /> <br /> 1) Healing neither helps your achieve your goals nor allows you to delay someone else achieving your goals. Sure, it keeps up the basic survival instinct of anyone, but it's an imperfect trade-off even on that front, because of Death Rage, and we'll get into that in a bit.<br /> <br /> 2) Your time in Gauru is possibly the most important resource you have for any strategic employment, because unlike some of the other resource where it can be easy to restore with creative or transgressive solutions, you have no way of extending your comfortable time in Gauru within a scene, and every turn not taking advantage of the way it turns things into shooting fish in a barrel (assuming you have made the barrel) is a turn that makes it bonfire where you need a welding torch, and not even on that burns anyone. Wasting those turns <i>just</i> to heal is not a good strategy, it's an indicator you've already fucking lost the battle and need to run the hell away, because.<br /> <br /> 3) Any discussion about the healing that does not also factor in Rage is pretty well so much noise in the rain, because it's not thinking about how the action economy matters for matters of combat and violent solutions to problems. So, for a recap, shifting into Gauru, for any reason, means your next turn has a total of four possible actions, being A) kill the motherfucker in front of your, B) throw something to try and kill the motherfucker you see down the way (which in a grand majority of cases is just not going to be as efficient as a combo of C and A), C) move closer to a motherfucker you're about to kill, and D) shift down. All of those, with reflexive exceptions for D that a grand majority of the time is going to eat into your Essence resources wastefully (particularly if you're constantly shifting up and down in combat), are going to eat up your turn for doing things that are going to be conducive towards establishing your scenario control that lets you use Gauru as the shotgun for a barrel of fish, particularly because.<br /> <br /> 4) Eating up your actions is already going to make you more of a target than you need to be, which is going to be important here in a bit, but making it worse is that, outside of the tightest of action economy management that still isn't all that helpful, everything about the way Rage emphasizes aggressive positioning is an overextension that puts you at greater risk unless you're in a position where it pays to just finish the follow through. It almost guarantees you're out in the open in some way when you DO manage to shift down, and with a whole turn for people to dump violence into you, that's not great.<br /> <br /> 5) This one is subjective, but I would make the argument that any Storyteller who has players who shift into Gauru <i>just to heal</i> is well within their right to call for a Death Rage roll.<br /> <br /> Now, on that turn thing...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's impossible to keep damage on a werewolf unless it's aggravated. </div> </div> </div><i>Not really</i>.<br /> <br /> I think the thing that trips people up on this is the term &quot;turn&quot; and how it's used everywhere else versus in Chronicles, so to lay it out directly, Chronicles uses the term &quot;turn&quot; the same way other games might use &quot;round&quot;. WHen you understand that, you get to see the problem-a round of people stabbing and/or shooting you (either decreasing your Defense every attack or never caring about it) racks up by the time it gets around to your turn, and frequently does so by converting around to Aggravated damage-and every point of Agg Damage makes that trip shorter. And because of that, it can be easy to fall into a trap of a sunk cost fallacy for survival purposes-because these people are stacking lethal into becoming aggravated damage, shifting down makes you more vulnerable to that lethal damage, so you have to stay in Gauru to survive, but in order to stay in that, you have to pursue aggressive action, which means you're likely to stay in a vulnerable location, which results in more damage. And smart opponents will get this and exploit to hell-and you don't get far in the world of Chronicles if you stay dumb.<br /> <br /> Gauru makes it easy to survive when you are breaking up the opposition in a way they'll prefer retreat against co-ordinated or overwhelming offense. It's a temptation to die outside of that circumstance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It creates the superman problem. Superman is impervious to all damage, so attacking him is pointless, unless you use the mcguffin (kryptonite/silver/whatever) which can put him down almost instantly. </div> </div> </div>Heavy Arms has already done a good job deconstructing this, but I want to succinctly suspect that you have either never watched any of the Superman cartoons/shows/movies* ongoing, or you've managed to forget just how much Superman gets challenged in his own media all the god damn time, no Kryptonite required. I'm also going to suggest that you're making the same mistake with Superman that people often make with combat in Chronicles, in assuming the violence is for violence's own sake and not for the purpose of <a href=\"https://youtu.be/RXdiCgBxNEQ\" target=\"_blank\">other purposes</a>. The Uratha, by comparison, are much squishier. If the problem is that players cannot come up with enough conflicts to challenge their character, while Superman has the better part of a century being relevant because of all the ways he's been challenged, maybe the problem is where the players are focusing. There's a reason Zak &quot;I dedicated Sucker Punch to my mom&quot; Snyder was a terrible choice for DC movies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So enemies are either pointless (no silver) or super deadly (with silver), there is no middle ground. </div> </div> </div>Or stabbed/shot a whole fucking bunch, which people are half as likely to do when someone erupts into a giant fuck you man-eating wolf as run the fuck away, and also, that run the fuck away instinct makes them less effective even in situation where people are not of the right mindset to kill a (unexpected) giant fuck you man-eating wolf, which is arguably a middle ground, but also-<br /> <br /> -any scenario that forces a player to consider Uratha as a viable answer <i>just for survival</i> is already a situation that is High Conflict that begs a question of no middle ground, because it should either be ....I dislike pointless, I'll suggest either negatively effortless, or super deadly. There is a mismanagement somewhere if this is not the case-and hey, we all learn, but by that, it pays to know where the fault lies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Werewolves in gauru form destroying everything around them? </div> </div> </div>I'm obliged to point out how this hits on the problem with the physical violence of Primal Fear-you can Down and Dirty combat people you can fight as appropriate for Rage in Gauru, which is hilariously potent when players are able to group up people who make up a large number of tertiary damage actions, but kind of a waste when you're only using it to instantly take down one person.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Actually they only have to attack an enemy, and only one that's still active. They never attack friends or innocents, and don't have to kill the enemy. If it acted more like a vampire's frenzy then maybe it would be ok. </div> </div> </div>I think I've already done a good job addressing the way that first line is half the problem, so for the rest of it:<br /> <br /> The thing of the matter, regarding not attacking friends, innocents, and not even needing to kill an enemy, is that a lot of this is true when you've taken the time to make Gauru form usage the most efficient you can, but when you're using it irresponsibly and inefficiently, you increasingly turn it into a game of chicken with disaster. Again, if the opponent is hitting you hard enough to make using Gauru for survival a seemingly viable answer, then you're facing rounds where trying to win is just locking you into more and more damage and bleeding turns until you run into Death Rage, and then you run exactly into that problem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3-5 round being nothing? What game are you playing? I don't think I've ever had a combat go past 3-4 rounds. This isn't D&amp;D, combat in CoD is fast. Simply evading and defending against a werewolf in gauru form for 5+ rounds is asking a hell of a lot, especially when you take some of the other bs werewolf combat gifts into account, and it makes for a long and boring combat if the enemy just dodges every round. </div> </div> </div>I feel like you've arrived at conventional number of rounds from the opposite end of operation, and the thing that makes me think this is the assumption that CofD is fast. Combat in Chronicles can feel fast because actions are weighty and impactful, and the game encourages you to take out the majority of opposition outside of the combat subsystem-but that goes both ways, and ill-advised action can easily drag out a conflict. THe way Gauru limits your options for action makes it so that, unless you make it something that you can invest in and end a combat with, is pretty apparently easy to kite and manipulate around, and any opposition that has an exit strategy is likely to notice or take advantage of it. Even panicked opponents are likely to make someone relying on Gauru casually run into a prolonged game of attrition by scattering and panic attacking to build up damage, and any opponent who has experience with the Uratha can and will make long scale attrition a meaningful barrier of death to a pack's goals and interests. Combat in Chronicles is &quot;fast&quot; because it usually has things slant in favor of one side or the other, and the main incentive of those who don't have it is to leave, regroup, and have another go-but when it gets into the thick of it, Chronicles combat can be a rather long affair, particularly if the opposition knows how to make things work in their favor -and most of the Uratha's prey have had ages to learn.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe if the healing thing was toned down, or it cost essense every round the werewolf remained in gauru form, or a werewolf in gauru form had to all-out attack every round (no defense), or the duration was much lower, or it could only be used once per chapter and not per scene, or the gauru had to attack uncontrollably rather than being able to focus on only enemies, any of these things would make it so much more balanced. And I'm talking about balanced as in against the game in general and what other splats can do. I know CoD plays it loose when it comes to game balance, but there are some things that are just unfairly strong and/or completely unbalanced. </div> </div> </div>Putting aside ideas for balance because I am suspicious of the lack of Chesterton's Fence going on, I feel like the need to frame Gauru's advantages in the context of Chronicles on the whole is rather revealing, because it points out an acknowledgement that Gauru is designed for the context of Forsaken and the sense that it somehow works there. Chronicles games have a wide disparity of power and forms-a crossover game can have people who throttle the heavens paired up with a guy who has a shotgun from that one time their cousin took them out shooting for their birthday- because the games are designed to work internally with itself first. There's a reason why crossover was held off as a major focus of the books for so long.<br /> <br /> Within the context of Forsaken, the Uratha's advantages, including Gauru, are weighted against opponents who have reasonable ways to challenge that toolset-the Claimed are vigorously tough and tend to have environmental advantages, the shartha play attrition better than anyone else, spirits are almost just as slippery, tend to have esoteric advantages that are hard to take advantage of, and have millenia of familiarity with the Uratha, other werewolf antagonists literally know the Forsaken's playbook. Humans are the most subject to an imbalance, but so much of their power is already rooted in the sociological power and impact, and the traits that make humanity the persistence predator they are in reality can come together to make their a very smart opponent against the Uratha when a storyteller is willing to remember those. Everything is appropriate for a game of Forsaken.<br /> <br /> Within the context of crossover, the overall imbalance is easily handled by remembering to <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0N2IiV6VMqU\" target=\"_blank\">pair threats to the scale of their impact </a>on the larger picture of what's happening-it doesn't matter if one person can throttle the heavens and one just has a shotgun if someone needs to hold back the heavens while someone else stops the bad guys or gets the thing. The Avengers movies, for whatever else can be said of those, provide good examples of how to do that, particularly the first one where consideration was very heavily payed to the fact that one of them could fucking shoot out massive fuck you bolts of lightning but another one of them was a a spy more specialized for taking out small groups of opponents. In crosssover, the Forsaken are upper tier powerhouses, arguably the fourth place winner in the overall power scale behind mages, mummies, and demons, and as such planning for them means understanding them as controlling more of the scenario and tanking against significant threats to open up other actors to make the significant tipping action. But, as grouping them with those other ones points out, this is not a unique problem for the Forsaken, nor is it a deal breaker.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's a difference between being strong and being broken, and garu form is leaning pretty heavy on the later. I guess when it comes to dealing with werewolves I'll just have to give everyone kryptonite, sorry I mean silver weapons. </div> </div> </div>The longest game I've ever run in Chronicle was a tier one game of Hunter: the Vigil, and I regard this as one of the most instructive experiences I've had with games, because figuring out tactics and strategies for how to fight monsters from a permanently uphill perspective means you really learn to think how handle problems. My players, two in number at the time, eventually took down a pack of werewolves without a single ounce of silver, and they did it by exploiting the limitations of the werewolves.<br /> <br /> Thinking through the problem, learning as much as you can, and planning around what you can is always going to be more lethal than a silver bullet.<br /> <br /> *I don't mention reading the comics cause that's not really where I've experienced Superman, but I've watched too much Superman &amp; Lois(90s), Superman &amp; Lois(new one), Supergirl(not originally CW but CW), Superman The Animated Series, Justice League(animated series), Superman(the Donner Series), Superman Returns, and Smallville to be anything but bored when people bust out this canard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 04-02-2023, 09:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-01T18:19:59-07:00","id":1507140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1498600-gauru-form-too-strong?p=1507116#post1507116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5) This one is subjective, but I would make the argument that any Storyteller who has players who shift into Gauru <i>just to heal</i> is well within their right to call for a Death Rage roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not even that subjective, I'd add \u2014 taking Gauru outside of combat is a universal Death Rage trigger, and if you're in Gauru when you enter Death Rage you skip straight from Wasu-Im to Basu-Im, where you're committed to being on a blackout murder spree for at least the next ten minutes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-02T06:29:27-07:00","id":1507178,"title":"","content":"Garou are <i>supposed </i>to be the powerhouses of Wod, aren't they?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-02T07:13:44-07:00","id":1507181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1498600-gauru-form-too-strong?p=1507178#post1507178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Garou are <i>supposed </i>to be the powerhouses of Wod, aren't they?</div> </div> </div> </div>This thread is about the Uratha in Gauru form, the Garou of WoD are something else entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-02T10:59:34-07:00","id":1507192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1498600-gauru-form-too-strong?p=1507178#post1507178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Garou are <i>supposed </i>to be the powerhouses of Wod, aren't they?</div> </div> </div> </div>We're in Chronicles land, not World....land.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-03T13:09:39-07:00","id":1507310,"title":"","content":"Gauru form isn't really all that overpowered, it lasts for 4 to 5 turns for a starting character and aside from the extra health and healing, you're not really given anything to mitigate oncoming damage. To be perfectly honest, for a time limited form I think it has a lot of drawbacks and actually goes down way to easily if anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27672-forsakenprospects","name":"ForsakenProspects","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27672_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-03T13:16:18-07:00","id":1507312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ForsakenProspects</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1498600-gauru-form-too-strong?p=1507310#post1507310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gauru form isn't really all that overpowered, it lasts for 4 to 5 turns for a starting character and aside from the extra health and healing, you're not really given anything to mitigate oncoming damage. To be perfectly honest, for a time limited form I think it has a lot of drawbacks and actually goes down way to easily if anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's incredibly potent...in the right circumstances. The biggest problem with it is that players tend to just treat it like a super mode, and storytellers don't plan accordingly for it or think through it's limitations to make it Not Always the Nominal Solution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-04T02:16:48-07:00","id":1507382,"title":"","content":"Again, average Uratha can keep Gauru for 3-4 turns. How is it OP?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T12:46:37-07:00","id":1515284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aurumae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1498600-gauru-form-too-strong?p=1507045#post1507045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Having played a fair bit of Forsaken 2e this was not my experience.<br /> <br /> Let's take for example the time our pack fought a pack of Pure. We caused the Pure pack to all death rage near the start of the combat (by murdering their totem). They all took Gauru form, and we mostly stayed in Dalu and Urshul form. We managed to wipe out the Pure pack without using any silver. How? By focusing on one enemy at a time. We used our gifts, positioning, and misdirection to make sure that most of the Pure were chasing after shadows and not able to bring their strength to bear. We then focused down one enemy before moving on to the next. A Gauru form Werewolf only heals their health track in lethal each turn - for most Werewolves this is going to be about 11 damage. Dealing 11 damage across 2-3 attacks in a turn is not very difficult. One thing we found useful was that you can make characters with lethal damage attack first in the round to fill up those 11 boxes. Any characters dealing bashing damage can then attack later in the same round and it will count as agg regardless. It took us about 2 rounds to take down each of the Pure using these tactics.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Aurumae, I find your posts extremely helpful in explaining the game. Could you elaborate how your Pack destroyed the Pure pack in Kuruth? I am curious about which tactics were used, as well as gifts and any tools","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T12:48:46-07:00","id":1515285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1498600-gauru-form-too-strong?p=1507116#post1507116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The longest game I've ever run in Chronicle was a tier one game of Hunter: the Vigil, and I regard this as one of the most instructive experiences I've had with games, because figuring out tactics and strategies for how to fight monsters from a permanently uphill perspective means you really learn to think how handle problems. My players, two in number at the time, eventually took down a pack of werewolves without a single ounce of silver, and they did it by exploiting the limitations of the werewolves.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>ArcaneArts, I find your posts and essays very helpful as well. I am curious how 2 hunters destroyed a pack of Uratha...without silver. Can you elaborate what those 2 hunters did?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T21:11:47-07:00","id":1515327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1498600-gauru-form-too-strong?p=1515284#post1515284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Aurumae, I find your posts extremely helpful in explaining the game. Could you elaborate how your Pack destroyed the Pure pack in Kuruth? I am curious about which tactics were used, as well as gifts and any tools</div> </div> </div> </div>It's been quite a few years so lets see how much I can remember.<br /> <br /> We went in with the knowledge that we intended to wipe out the pack. They had been causing a bunch of problems for us and were up to some shenanigans in the Shadow that we wanted to put a stop to. Our plan going in was to distract them while two of our packmates took out their totem. Their totem was a huge phoenix type thing, and was way more powerful than ours. It was also responsible for the issues in the Shadow - they were setting the whole Shadow in the area on fire and had some kind of cult of humans they were using to empower the totem.<br /> <br /> The Pure were set up in a church, and their totem was on top of the church. If I remember correctly, we actually attacked them in the Shadow. Our Rahu and our Ithaeur (group A) snuck off to take down the totem, while the Cahalith (myself) the Elodoth and the Irraka (group B) took on the Pure pack assisted by our own Totem. Before launching the attack, I used This Story Is True to empower our Elodoth who didn't have a high brawl skill, and Song in Your Heart to empower the whole pack. We had also called a Siskur-Dah on the totem and most of us were using our Auspice 3 abilities (the ones that give you big bonuses on the Siskur-Dah).<br /> <br /> Group B launched the attack first to draw their attention. My character had a really high defense (I had 6 dots in athletics thanks to our totem advantage, and 4-6 dots in dexterity depending on form, so up to 12 defense), so the plan was basically to get them to focus their attacks on me in the opening stages. The Elodoth had Memento Mori, so the idea was that he would hang back, and if any of us took a lot of damage he would siphon the damage away. I think we went in to attack in Urshul and Dalu form, and as soon as the battle was joined I used War Howl (which was also the signal for group A to go).<br /> <br /> I think the Pure pack were initially pretty cautious, staying in Hishu or just taking Dalu form. I was basically blocking the doorway to the church so that was where the fighting started, with the Pure focusing on me as intended. One of the Pure hung back inside the church and was using Gifts to empower her packmates, so the Irraka decided to use her batman powers to take her out. The Irraka had some absolutely obscene weaponry dice pool with knives, and our Rahu had blessed the knives using Perfection of Form before we went to the attack. The outcome was that the knives had 8-again and something like 6 bonus successes on the first attack. Combine that with the rote action from Eviscerate and the result was that one of the Pure went from perfect health to something like 1 agg away from death in a single hit.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile the group on the roof were closing in on the totem. The whole time the totem had been flying around, raining fire down on us, and our own totem had been staying hidden as best it could. The Ithaeur used Shadow Gaze on the totem and learned that its ban and bane. I think the bane was Holy Water, which would have been handy had we not been in the Shadow. In any case, the Ithaeur was noticed and started taking the brunt of the totem's attacks, but he was protected by Shadow Hunter from the worst of it. The Rahu though was still unnoticed, and we then had a really cinematic moment where the Rahu leapt from the top of the church in Gauru form right on top of this blazing phoenix and tackled it straight to the ground below. The totem was then surrounded, with the Pure pack bottled up inside the church and most of our Pack still outside around it on the ground. We basically dogpiled it and tore it apart (getting a decent amount of essence back in the process).<br /> <br /> The ST decided that this counted as a Kuruth trigger and had the Pure pack all make rolls. All but one failed and went into death rage. Interestingly, I think with the death of their totem they technically no longer counted as a Pack for the purpose of Gifts etc. but it didn't end up mattering.<br /> <br /> I had taken a few sharp knocks by that point and was now facing down multiple Gauru, so I backed out into the area in front of the Church and took Gauru for a turn myself in order to heal. I think I might have had 2 or 3 agg which the Elodoth helped by taking a point on himself. The Pure came barrelling out of the Church, and we used the fact that they had to attack an opponent within striking range each turn to control who they would go after. One thing to note is that Gauru form has +4 speed while Urshul has +7, so by being able to choose our forms we could easily stay ahead of them. Our totem helped out too and I think it ended up getting discorporated by the end of the fight, but for the most part it was able to zoom around at high speed (it had speed 20 I think) throwing out Blasts with the Gauru chasing after it. Inside the Church the Irraka finished off the wounded Pure pack member. She then joined the fight outside and was able to use Hit and Run on the Gauru to deal some serious damage to them and then avoid reprisal.<br /> <br /> We took the enemies down one by one, focusing on whoever looked like they were weak that turn while denying the Pure the opportunity to do the same to us. We took some hard knocks, but by the end of the fight the only one left in their pack was the one who hadn't death raged, and he ran off. During the fight we made full use of our Gifts - I used Primal Strength as did the Rahu. I used Thousand Throat Howl to Demoralize them. The Irraka used Stealth and Evasion Gifts to use Eviscerate again and again. The Rahu used Killer Instinct to get some incredible brawl dice pools. We made use of our Auspice Benefits - the Irraka used <i>Closer Than You Thought</i> to suddenly appear behind the Pure in the Church and nearly one-shotted her (which I think was crucial to us winning, we knew that Pure had access to some scary Gifts), and our Elodoth used his ability to pull one of the Pure out of Death Rage - thus forcing him down into a weaker form <i>and</i> inflicting the Stunned tilt, which we were able to capitalise on. Furthermore, we all took Gauru at one point or another in order to heal or do a big attack, but avoided the form otherwise and were able to avoid death raging ourselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2384,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","user":"Aurumae","date":". 06-17-2023, 12:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-18T00:15:34-07:00","id":1515446,"title":"","content":"Mechanical considerations aside there is also story reasons restricting the use of Gauru, such as character goals.<br /> To drag out the tired Superman example again if Kal's goal was to find out who was responsible for the dastardly deed and then rip their head off, Luthor is a one shot villain turned corpse, but its not, the goal is to find out who is responsible for the dastardly deed and then take them down using the criminal justice system.<br /> Here Kal can't use his super strength to fight Luthor's connections <br /> (At the time I was having dinner with the Governor)<br /> his organization <br /> (All of your evidence is circumstantial, there is nothing here that directly ties Mr Luthor to the crime)<br /> and finally plain old corruption<br /> (What do you mean the judge threw out the evidence, what about the witness...Police Officer: we are dragging Hobb's bay, don't hold your breath.)<br /> <br /> For Werewolves their goals almost always revolve aroung their territory, so if the goal is to fill it with ruined buildings, a fleeing citizenry and a glut of fear and death spirits then Gauru is the perfect tool. If the goal is anything else then a little more discretion is probably best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-18T08:47:28-07:00","id":1515460,"title":"","content":"Referencing the last 2 posts, evasion seems to be the key to surviving the garou form. Either dodging (which doubles your defense pool), having a higher speed and running away, using Evasion gifts ( Hit and Run seems useful), celerity, wall climbing, burrow, discorporate...etc. The Hosts even have a built in Discorporate power which is an automatic escape route if the hunt wasn't prepared perfectly in advance.<br /> <br /> Also the social consequences of Garou can be severe. The book hints that a hunter compact formed in Detroit due to the lunacy. In addition, the Shadow Shadows in the Spirit section suggests that they form when the lunacy affects a community.<br /> <br /> Many times it seems that the improper use of Garou creates more problems than it solves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-19T15:52:54-07:00","id":1515576,"title":"","content":"If what you are after is a way to challenge werewolves that is not immediately bested by Garou, then my experience has been the secret is not to attack the wolves but their territory. When a fire spirit shows up in their territory it shouldn't start a bonfire, scream out its challenge and then go out in a blaze of glory battling the pack. Instead its presence should be announce with an uptick of arson cases, children playing with matches and normal fires suddenly raging out of control. Force the pack to hunt it and when they finally confront and defeat it, even if the battle is somewhat easy, the pain it caused them should leave them feeling mighty satisfied to have gutted it.<br /> <br /> Also sometimes killing your enemy isn't the best answer because sometimes that enemy is actually your friend, if it keeps its place. Especially when it comes to Spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-19T19:01:55-07:00","id":1515605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1498600-gauru-form-too-strong?p=1515576#post1515576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When a fire spirit shows up in their territory it shouldn't start a bonfire, scream out its challenge and then go out in a blaze of glory battling the pack.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's worth noting even if they do this it doesn't mean the spirit is dead. Spirits are awesome because even having lost the fight to a Gauru form Uratha they can typically come back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-20T01:30:09-07:00","id":1515629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1498600-gauru-form-too-strong?p=1515605#post1515605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's worth noting even if they do this it doesn't mean the spirit is dead. Spirits are awesome because even having lost the fight to a Gauru form Uratha they can typically come back.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless it is the target of the Siskur-Dah.<br /> <br /> Spirits typically fear Werewolves because they have this trick in their back pocket that can permanently kill them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-27T06:29:10-07:00","id":1523205,"title":"","content":"Sorry to resurrect this topic, but it is too much fun to talk about.<br /> <br /> Has anyone mentioned Cannibalism or Ufarah's Bane? The Uratha bite can cause aggravated damage, and with the huge amount of damage that Uratha can cause, I imagine that a pack vs. pack fight between Uratha can be finished very quickly. Sure their harmony will go to hell, and there will be numerous violations of the Oath of the Moon, but the fight will be over quickly.<br /> <br /> That said, does Cannibalism only apply to the Forsaken? Do The Pure, Bale Hounds, and Ghost Wolves care if they descend to madness. I figure the Predator Kings would be perfectly fine biting their enemies to cause aggravated damange.<br /> <br /> The Rite Ufarah's Bane is similar, without all the violations of the Oath of the Moon.<br /> <br /> Once you factor this in, the Garou form is really just extra health levels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-27T06:48:16-07:00","id":1523206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1498600-gauru-form-too-strong?p=1523205#post1523205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry to resurrect this topic, but it is too much fun to talk about.<br /> <br /> Has anyone mentioned Cannibalism or Ufarah's Bane? The Uratha bite can cause aggravated damage, and with the huge amount of damage that Uratha can cause, I imagine that a pack vs. pack fight between Uratha can be finished very quickly. Sure their harmony will go to hell, and there will be numerous violations of the Oath of the Moon, but the fight will be over quickly.<br /> <br /> That said, does Cannibalism only apply to the Forsaken? Do The Pure, Bale Hounds, and Ghost Wolves care if they descend to madness. I figure the Predator Kings would be perfectly fine biting their enemies to cause aggravated damange.<br /> <br /> The Rite Ufarah's Bane is similar, without all the violations of the Oath of the Moon.<br /> <br /> Once you factor this in, the Garou form is really just extra health levels.</div> </div> </div> </div>The pure have their own version of the Oath of the Moon and it does indeed forbid cannibalism. The Oaths also forbids the murder of other Uratha to begin with, no matter if cannibalism is involved or not. The book even calls out that while there is much discussion about the differences between killing and murder that any killing of Uratha is a sin against harmony. But also don't forget, there's an entire tribe who have other Uratha as their favored enemy. <br /> <br /> Also, Uratha do not &quot;descend to madness&quot; for breaking the Oath of the Moon (or the pure equivalent) instead they have sinned against harmony. They may become more spirit like, but that's not going mad.<br /> <br /> A more serious issue if you break the oath of the moon is punishment. You can face a lot of punishment, up to exile or the loss of limbs for breaking the oath of the moon in committing cannibalism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-27T06:57:35-07:00","id":1523207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1498600-gauru-form-too-strong?p=1523205#post1523205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Uratha bite can cause aggravated damage</div> </div> </div> </div> when eating humans and wolves to gain Essence. Basically like an extreme form of gorging on Essence from something Resonant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-27T07:52:20-07:00","id":1523210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1498600-gauru-form-too-strong?p=1523205#post1523205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry to resurrect this topic, but it is too much fun to talk about.<br /> <br /> Has anyone mentioned Cannibalism or Ufarah's Bane? The Uratha bite can cause aggravated damage, and with the huge amount of damage that Uratha can cause, I imagine that a pack vs. pack fight between Uratha can be finished very quickly. Sure their harmony will go to hell, and there will be numerous violations of the Oath of the Moon, but the fight will be over quickly.<br /> <br /> That said, does Cannibalism only apply to the Forsaken? Do The Pure, Bale Hounds, and Ghost Wolves care if they descend to madness. I figure the Predator Kings would be perfectly fine biting their enemies to cause aggravated damange.<br /> <br /> The Rite Ufarah's Bane is similar, without all the violations of the Oath of the Moon.<br /> <br /> Once you factor this in, the Garou form is really just extra health levels.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Cannibalism bit really needed some to be fleshed out more in my opinion. It's only mentioned in the section on gaining essence and leaves a lot of questions - why can't the Uratha eat the corpus of Spirits for example? In fact rules as written it only works on wolves and humans, so it doesn't even effect other Werewolves. I don't actually buy this take, but I think it's a good example of the fact that this rule needed to be given more of a write-up.<br /> <br /> Personally I don't actually like this rule very much. I'm all for powering up Werewolves, but 2e seemed to make a very deliberate decision that if Werewolves want to deal agg damage they <i>have</i> to use banes (including vs other Werewolves, via Silver). Nonetheless, if we are going to keep this rule it should probably have been some kind of separate action, like the feed move is in Vampire. I think it would also have helped to bring all the special effects tied to Werewolves natural weapons together in one place - they deal lethal to Vampires (I would extend this to other splats that downgrade mundane damage, such as Mummies), they deal agg to lower rank Spirits, and they can use this special move to deal agg to humans and wolves (and I would add Werewolves and most human-like splats to this).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-27T09:27:46-07:00","id":1523213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aurumae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1498600-gauru-form-too-strong?p=1523210#post1523210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Cannibalism bit really needed some to be fleshed out more in my opinion. It's only mentioned in the section on gaining essence and leaves a lot of questions - why can't the Uratha eat the corpus of Spirits for example? In fact rules as written it only works on wolves and humans, so it doesn't even effect other Werewolves. I don't actually buy this take, but I think it's a good example of the fact that this rule needed to be given more of a write-up.<br /> <br /> Personally I don't actually like this rule very much. I'm all for powering up Werewolves, but 2e seemed to make a very deliberate decision that if Werewolves want to deal agg damage they <i>have</i> to use banes (including vs other Werewolves, via Silver). Nonetheless, if we are going to keep this rule it should probably have been some kind of separate action, like the feed move is in Vampire. I think it would also have helped to bring all the special effects tied to Werewolves natural weapons together in one place - they deal lethal to Vampires (I would extend this to other splats that downgrade mundane damage, such as Mummies), they deal agg to lower rank Spirits, and they can use this special move to deal agg to humans and wolves (and I would add Werewolves and most human-like splats to this).</div> </div> </div> </div>You're welcome to talk about house ruling stuff all you want, but I do want to point out that by the rules Uratha's natural weapons do not deal lethal damage to vampires, their bite deals lethal damage to vampires, and not just vampires but all creatures vulnerable to mystical damage so it is extended to splats that downgrade &quot;mundane damage&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-27T11:27:04-07:00","id":1523224,"title":"","content":"A useful clarification comes from the sidebar, The Predator's Jaws, on page 98 of the Werewolf: the Forsaken Second Edition corebook.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uratha bite to kill. Their teeth carry the deadly resonance of Father Wolf, the ultimate hunter. As such, their bites in every form count as mystical sources to foes that are vulnerable to such sources. Even in Hishu, a werewolf\u2019s bite causes lethal damage to vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>THere's a thread that got into the weeds of it-I'm not reviewing all of it because it's a lot and I have things to do, but one of the main writers <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/122291-uratha-teeth-and-claws?p=124366#post124366\">explains the logic the team went with</a>, and if I recall, Stew and Rose pop in to confirm their collaboration on the choices about werewolf lethality.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Okay, I did have a quick glance to spot the relevant team members, the other asides from Bunyip being strider(Jim FIscher) and MachineIV(Olivia Hill).<br /> <br /> They do talk about a werewolf's claws, but Werewolf was still in development at the time, so it's likely they found confining the benefit to the teeth a reasonable compromise, though I am still quick scanning the book on that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-27-2023, 02:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-27T11:51:57-07:00","id":1523225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1498600-gauru-form-too-strong?p=1523205#post1523205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry to resurrect this topic, but it is too much fun to talk about.<br /> <br /> Has anyone mentioned Cannibalism or Ufarah's Bane? The Uratha bite can cause aggravated damage, and with the huge amount of damage that Uratha can cause, I imagine that a pack vs. pack fight between Uratha can be finished very quickly. Sure their harmony will go to hell, and there will be numerous violations of the Oath of the Moon, but the fight will be over quickly.<br /> <br /> That said, does Cannibalism only apply to the Forsaken? Do The Pure, Bale Hounds, and Ghost Wolves care if they descend to madness. I figure the Predator Kings would be perfectly fine biting their enemies to cause aggravated damange.<br /> <br /> The Rite Ufarah's Bane is similar, without all the violations of the Oath of the Moon.<br /> <br /> Once you factor this in, the Garou form is really just extra health levels.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what these have to do with the overall subject of the Gauru form being overpowered or not.<br /> <br /> Cannibalism is more likely a concern in Death Rage, though it's easier to commit to it (and justify it) in Gauru if a werewolf wants to, and Urfarah's Bane is a Rite that is generally designed for murder within their own spheres(on the subject of vampires, I would argue that the clarification it's &quot;werewolves only&quot; caveat can be muddled with and argued if one really wants to at their table).<br /> <br /> The Pure suffer the Harmony hit for cannibalism same as the Forsaken-it pays to remember that the Oaths of the Moon and Urfarah respectively are more codifications to help each set of tribes understand the consequences of their own Harmony rather actual oaths, as opposed to the Tribal Oaths which <i>do</i> alter a werewolf's spiritual makeup. This is why Ghost Wolves also suffer the cannibalism hit. The Bale Hounds, by contrast....well, one fifth of them are built on cannibalism as a principle, and the rest aren't far behind thanks to the Rite of Absolution.<br /> <br /> Gauru's not more than just extra health levels-the combat thread I linked to back a page or so makes a point of how potent the whole kit is-but it's also not the absolute solution the rest of this thread makes it out to be. It's the answer when the rest of the work is done, the quickest way to tie up all the loose ends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-27T12:36:09-07:00","id":1523230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1498600-gauru-form-too-strong?p=1523225#post1523225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Bale Hounds, by contrast....well, one fifth of them are built on cannibalism as a principle, and the rest aren't far behind thanks to the Rite of Absolution.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's strikes me now that you mention it, it seems like Bale Hounds are supposed to be &quot;the worst&quot; of the Uratha, yet so many of the Forsaken institutions are build around the same things, like cannibalism. Lodge of the Field is all about it, Eaters of the Dead are commanded to engage in it if they kill a human (or anything else that counts), Ghost Wolf Devourers focus on it, it could be the breaking point a ghost wolf tyrant uses, etc. I mean I guess, technically, those are all ghost wolf things and ghost wolves can be Forsaken or Pure, but Ghost Wolves always just strike me as generally being on the Forsaken side, probably since they're playable out of the main book rather than needing Shunned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-27T13:01:54-07:00","id":1523232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1498600-gauru-form-too-strong?p=1523230#post1523230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's strikes me now that you mention it, it seems like Bale Hounds are supposed to be &quot;the worst&quot; of the Uratha, yet so many of the Forsaken institutions are build around the same things, like cannibalism. Lodge of the Field is all about it, Eaters of the Dead are commanded to engage in it if they kill a human (or anything else that counts), Ghost Wolf Devourers focus on it, it could be the breaking point a ghost wolf tyrant uses, etc. I mean I guess, technically, those are all ghost wolf things and ghost wolves can be Forsaken or Pure, but Ghost Wolves always just strike me as generally being on the Forsaken side, probably since they're playable out of the main book rather than needing Shunned.</div> </div> </div> </div>Welcome to Chronicles of Darkness! You're the monster.<br /> <br /> Joking about facts asides, this came up as a particular point a few years when (I think) the latest iteration of the &quot;Good Pure&quot; argument rolled out, and the writers (again, Bunyip primarily) made the point that the morality of Forsaken Second Editions was <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1382725-decent-anshega?p=1383902#post1383902\">generally darker and more neutral</a> than it had been in First Edition. The Uratha are monsters that are, by and large, divorced for human psychology and social mores by their own being, and are generally motivated by a sort of blue-and-orange morality. To be blunt, being a serial killer is what they <i>do</i>. The Forsaken have no compulsion to be the best versions of werewolves out there, and the Pure, though easily motivated to be worse, have leeway in terms of their oaths, priorities, and sacred prey that allows them to be quite heroic, or at least more situationally ready to be the more &quot;moral&quot; between themselves and the Forsaken<br /> <br /> The Bales Hounds do remain exceptional, because they have incentive to take things to their most excessive when they can and to motivate and manipulate others into the same excess, but the general point is that Forsaken, in contrast to it's earlier fan positioning, is not secretly a game about darkly shaded heroes and good guys. THe Uratha are hunters, harrassers, and killers who hunt, harass, and kill in the name of shaping their territory into what they will it to be. Just because the Forsaken <i>sounds</i> nicer doesn't necessarily mean they <i>are.</i><br /> <br /> EDIT: THough of note, that same writer pointed out the ways in which <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1262140-pure-in-2e?p=1263155#post1263155\">the Pure were in deep denial</a>, so if that's something you hold against a group, then it's a thing to factor in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-27-2023, 04:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-27T16:56:21-07:00","id":1523240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1498600-gauru-form-too-strong?p=1523225#post1523225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure what these have to do with the overall subject of the Gauru form being overpowered or not.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that the Garou form makes an Uratha almost impervious to Bashing and Lethal damage, and Kuruth can extend the time limit a great deal. My point is that Aggravated wounds stick, and Cannibalism is an aggravated wounds tool all Uratha have. It is the equivalent of bringing a gun to a knife fight. It sidesteps the awkward debates of 2 Uratha hitting each other and not causing damage, and can end a fight very quickly.<br /> <br /> I agree the rules are a bit fuzzy. Page 71 says that Cannibalism leads to exile, yet page 285 says its a way to stop a raging werewolf in Kuruth. Does that mean that you get exiled and hunted by the Blood Talons because you had to kill a pack mate in Death Rage? I dunno. My theory is that it was a rule specifically designed to allow werewolf fights to be settled quickly, but its just a theory.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, it does seem to happen, the Ivory Claw hunter on page 199 seems to do it, as do the Lodge of the Field in Poland ( with some Blood Talons indulging as well). Also the Cull Ghost Wolves and hounds of consumption...<br /> <br /> It might just be that all Uratha are all monsters and must make a huge effort to prevent falling into Zir. So a Blood talon with high Purity must not only abstain from cannibalism, but must not even kill his prey on page 30. Werewolves probably must resist the temptation at all times, and their struggle is to keep their harmony intact and honor the Oath.<br /> <br /> Which brings brings us to Urfara's Bane and Silver. More expensive and tricky to weaponize silver, and Urara's Bane is a level 5 rite, but both are probably more acceptable than cannibalism","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-27T17:45:45-07:00","id":1523245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1498600-gauru-form-too-strong?p=1523213#post1523213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're welcome to talk about house ruling stuff all you want, but I do want to point out that by the rules Uratha's natural weapons do not deal lethal damage to vampires, their bite deals lethal damage to vampires, and not just vampires but all creatures vulnerable to mystical damage so it is extended to splats that downgrade &quot;mundane damage&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>My mistake.<br /> <br /> I do think the claws should play by the same rules though. Not for any reason of power - the teeth already do more damage in Urshul and Urhan and establish free grapples to boot. The reason I houserule Werewolf claws to share these benefits is simply for some variety - since the teeth are so much better most werewolf players take bite as a brawl specialty, and every fight is just Werewolves biting things, the claws being totally ignored. Giving the claws a bit more parity with bite allows things to be a bit more varied.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-27T17:58:44-07:00","id":1523246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1498600-gauru-form-too-strong?p=1523240#post1523240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would say that the Garou form makes an Uratha almost impervious to Bashing and Lethal damage, and Kuruth can extend the time limit a great deal. My point is that Aggravated wounds stick, and Cannibalism is an aggravated wounds tool all Uratha have. It is the equivalent of bringing a gun to a knife fight. It sidesteps the awkward debates of 2 Uratha hitting each other and not causing damage, and can end a fight very quickly.<br /> <br /> I agree the rules are a bit fuzzy. Page 71 says that Cannibalism leads to exile, yet page 285 says its a way to stop a raging werewolf in Kuruth. Does that mean that you get exiled and hunted by the Blood Talons because you had to kill a pack mate in Death Rage? I dunno. My theory is that it was a rule specifically designed to allow werewolf fights to be settled quickly, but its just a theory.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not strictly a rules issue. Remember there is no unified Forsaken Nation like the Garou Nation. If no one knows cannibalism happened except the person's own pack then their elodoth can set their punishment and they don't automatically have to involve anyone else. On the flip side of you eat an elder Forsaken's face in front of 5 different packs you will likely be held responsible by those same packs. <br /> <br /> I do wish it had gone more into exile as a punishment. Like I get if the Elodoth has the Cahalith inform the lunes you're screwed but if they don't then the exile can probably find a home not terribly far away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-27T19:13:40-07:00","id":1523248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1498600-gauru-form-too-strong?p=1523240#post1523240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Page 71 says that Cannibalism leads to exile,</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 71 says that the worst sins against the Oath \u2014 &quot;defiling the honor of the Forsaken and the Oath's very meaning&quot; \u2014 merits the worst punishments, of which exile is an example, and the examples of that type of sin include deliberately exposing the People to humanity or betraying your pack to the enemy. Cannibalism is discussed in the paragraph before, where the punishment tends to be harsh penance which may include being cast out of your pack and tribe \u2014 being stripped of your belonging to a group or society is different from being <i>run out of town</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-30T17:29:02-07:00","id":1523383,"title":"","content":"Silver is the most obvious balance against the Garou form. It is basically like Kryptonite to the Uratha, only is much more common. The most obvious ways to weaponize silver seem to be shot and hollowpoint filler, though there must be other clever applications.<br /> <br /> It has also the double whammy of dealing aggravated damage and being a Kuruth trigger (which is worse?). Squads of men in body armor carrying shotguns loaded with silver seem a good way to remind the Uratha who the apex predators are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-30T23:19:37-07:00","id":1523390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1498600-gauru-form-too-strong?p=1523383#post1523383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Silver is the most obvious balance against the Garou form. It is basically like Kryptonite to the Uratha, only is much more common. The most obvious ways to weaponize silver seem to be shot and hollowpoint filler, though there must be other clever applications.<br /> <br /> It has also the double whammy of dealing aggravated damage and being a Kuruth trigger (which is worse?). Squads of men in body armor carrying shotguns loaded with silver seem a good way to remind the Uratha who the apex predators are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Silver is also fairly expensive, and because of that it's hard to make a weapon with it designed for reusability-and all of that becomes excessive with a squad of men (presumeably trained by your framing) with body armor and shotguns.**<br /> <br /> Let's run with some averages here. For any game, the common player is usually not gonna have a Attribute outside of the realm of 1 through 3, particularly if they're trying to balance optimization with variety-3 dice, as a quick rule of thumb, is mostly reliable enough to get 1 success, which is all you need in the vein of keeping it simple, and while investment in the fourth and fifth dot of any given attribute can make it easy to keep skill costs down low and thus have more variety, it's more practical to have a solid dice pool or the better part of a dice pool built in at the base with Attributes where each dot has more lateral usage. Since Forsaken is a very Physical game, let's set our average at 3 for our average here for the relevant point of Stamina. If you then account for what Garou gives our lad for just taking damage, our Uratha has 12 Health Boxes (not including merits, because that gets so variable I'm not willing to call any particular a usable average, so that's 5 for initial, 3 for Stamina, and 4 for the combined matter of Gauru's Stamina and Size boost). For attack purposes, we'll also assume he has Strength 3 and Brawl 3, so in Gauru he's got a dice pool of 9, and since I'm not going beyond a turn for the purpose of illustration, I'll also have them spend Willpower to get 12, getting regularly 4 successes off of the die pool and 6 once we add in the bonus from claws and teeth, and we're gonna be generous and assume that our werewolf can reach any given shooter in 1 move action.<br /> <br /> For our shooters, let's assume you're talking about people who are not only trained in shooting but are also used to working with each other as a unit-that latter part isn't going to really come up, but I want to preface it to make it clear how much worse this assumption could gets. So, for our purposes, let's assume 3 for Dex, 3 for Firearms, with a statistical likelihood of two successes regularly, one as a near guarentee. And they're using shotguns, which in both the Chronicles core book and Hurt lock adds 3 Successes to any successful Firearms rolled for the purposes of shooting someone with said, and is also a 9-again*. I'm not assuming these guys are hunters, but I am assuming they're at least used to having to keep cool when shit's going down, and in fact for our basic assumption here, I'm openly going to assume idiocy because I want to make a point about raw numbers without tactical consideration, and I bring this all up because I think facing a giant fucking wolf-man from your nightmares warrants a Willpower expenditure on their parts, so we're looking at a basic dice pool of 9 dice. We'll also not be nice and assume they each have 2 Stamina, for 7 Health. And just to keep it simple, let's assume we have three of these guys.<br /> <br /> If our shooters, standing around like numbnuts, and at a bare minimum manage to just get 1 success each, these guys are still in just a turn delivering a full round of Lethal Hitboxes for our werewolf. Sure, he'll shrug that off on the next turn, but that's already Not Good. If we make a likelihood of just two successes each during one turn of shooting, our werewolf has 3 Aggravated Damage that's not going away, a full fourth of his extended health bar. Make it the actual statistical average of 3, and that's half of our Werewolf's bar gone in a turn that will not heal like that. And if any of those 9-Agains manages to land an additional success, that explodes even more. Even if you were to downgrade to Brief Nightmares and ran these guys as Minions so their best dice pool was 5 flat, it still demonstrates just how much three guys with shotguns can do.<br /> <br /> And then our werewolf gets to go in the turn, presumably healing all remaining Lethal Damage but very probably smarting bad. They run up to one guy, rolls, hits and gets out that 6 successes we established. If we just assume Kevlar Vests, that means 1 Person takes 5 Lethal, giving them a -1 to actions but still alive. It's not even that if we assume Flak Jackets or better, because that drops it down to a minimum of 4 or worse.<br /> <br /> And then very likely, in this incredibly stupid setup, it goes again and maybe one of them dies depending on the initative order, which is a nice moral victory before the werewolf goes bye bye. <hr />Now, as I kept iterating, this is a very stupid situation***, and I made it that way just to create a sense of the numbers at play with the proposed scenario and what relying on Gauru alone to survive looks like, but I also want you to consider what happens when you start including tactics into the matter, or even just changes in numbers. For our werewolves, there's obviously group tactics, Merits, Gifts, Rites benefits, and more, but for our humans it also includes their own tactics (and Tactics, if Hunters) and Merits. There's a lot of variables to really account for-are your shooters actually that decently trained, or are they more likely to run away in a scattered fashion or shoot in a haphazard way? Do those create accidental advantages? Werewolves like to operate together, but even on a focused hunt, there's oft-times where each is off doing their own individual thing, so are they being caught on their own? Is the fight happening in a place where the shooters have a lot of control, where there may be traps or security devices working to their aid? Did our shooters retreat and then do tactical surveillance to get an idea of their opposition's advantages in advance, or even start by doing that without a run in? How much of any of these apply to our werewolves in kind?<br /> <br /> This is why so much of the Uratha's tactics- as dictated by their Merits, Gifts, and Rites- includes controlling for <i>so many</i> of those variables as possible.\u200b That really dumb numbers game is <i>why</i> both sides need to think smartly about what they're doing and how much they have stacked in their favor-and just simply using Gauru as a win button clearly isn't that against any credible threat.<br /> <br /> TL;DR, any take on Gauru being overpowered without accounting for the actual numbers and variables is not a credible take.<br /> <br /> EDIT: also didn't account for Lunacy, again, going for numbers here as a basis to make it clear you can make a lot of arguments against the idiot argument which then basically makes it clear you have to account for the whos, whats, wheres, whens, whys, and hows of any given conflict.<br /> EDIT: also, going the other way, I didn't factor in the shooter's defense, honestly because I forgot, but also because that really doesn't help our werewolf out that much,<br /> <br /> *For just running estimatations, I treat the -Again rules as being in effect on 3/2/1 successes aspect-with 10-again, I need three successes before I assume a die is added, for 9-again, I need two, and for 8, every success adds a die, and from there the old standard of 3 Dice=1 Success. The Agains, in the way, aren't the most productive things in the universe, but they can be swingy.<br /> **If you want a more cost effective but very helpful solution, consider rock salt shells that inflict penalties with each one fired.<br /> ***without anymore additional context but trying to guess a reasonably smart situation where these people realize the other side as a threat suddenly but not in any way that grants surprise, our lone werewolf would more likely bolt taking advantage of either Urhan (for the size) or Urshul (for the speed)[assuming, of course, that our werewolf is not specced to bluff and lie their way into seeming like they belong there even if they are unexpected, or even just surrendering if the scenario lets it be advantageous], and our shooters will ward with their shots but not particularly directly chase the person what became a wolf, instead preferring to contact additional support to whatever end is most productive for what they're doing. A werewolf might take Gauru with the intent to scare off the shooters, but I would wager a scared-but-trained shooter set would retreat and otherwise try to sweep the legs, which they are very capable of doing and thus have a lot of benefit for escaping. Getting anymore specific is getting into the weeds but will invariably prove my point about Gauru <i>by itself</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-01-2023, 01:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-01T08:15:35-07:00","id":1523418,"title":"","content":"Make a Mage-backed organization of wanna-be Witchers, armed with Lunargent :P<br /> <br /> Sure, that only solves the Silver-as-a-weapon problem, but hey, better than nothing.<br /> <br /> Actually, would silver(Lunargent) armor be of any use? A Werewolf's strength can probably still pulp you, but unless they use a weapon they'd still have to touch it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-01T08:54:56-07:00","id":1523422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1498600-gauru-form-too-strong?p=1523418#post1523418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, would silver(Lunargent) armor be of any use? A Werewolf's strength can probably still pulp you, but unless they use a weapon they'd still have to touch it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless they don't have an auspice, simply touching silver isn't enough to deal damage to a werewolf:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WtF2e Core, p101, &quot;Silver&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A non-damaging touch with silver doesn\u2019t cause damage, but causes intense pain so long as the werewolf remains in contact, and leaves lasting scars as if from aggravated wounds.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WtF2e Core, p198</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pure werewolves suffer a greater reaction to silver than Forsaken do. Simply touching silver deals one point of bashing damage per turn and, under nights of the full moon, this is increased to one point of lethal damage.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-01T11:27:10-07:00","id":1523429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1498600-gauru-form-too-strong?p=1523383#post1523383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Silver is the most obvious balance against the Garou form. It is basically like Kryptonite to the Uratha, only is much more common. The most obvious ways to weaponize silver seem to be shot and hollowpoint filler, though there must be other clever applications.<br /> <br /> It has also the double whammy of dealing aggravated damage and being a Kuruth trigger (which is worse?). Squads of men in body armor carrying shotguns loaded with silver seem a good way to remind the Uratha who the apex predators are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. In fact I would say that squads of men in body armour tend to be such a low threat to competent Uratha that Gauru form is hardly even needed. I've seen this play out in game and all it takes is one Gift to put the Shadow Paranoia condition on the mortals and things will quickly start to fall apart. You also have to consider the environment and initiative. If the environment is an any way close (like a city street) the high initiatives and high speeds of the Uratha often mean that they can close the gap, attack, and inflict a bite and a grapple all in the same action turn before the guys with guns can react. Once grappled the guns are of little use. Combine that with Irraka taking out snipers using <i>Closer Than You Thought</i> and everyone rolling for lunacy as soon as a Dalu, Gauru or Urshul enters the fight and an orderly hit on the Werewolves quickly turns into chaos. Hit And Run, Fog of War, Berserker's Might, Unmake, and more can all render those expensive silver-loaded weapons useless, at least for long enough for them not to matter much in the outcome.<br /> <br /> Now if you send enough guys in can they do it? Sure, but I would argue that the point at which you have so many attackers that the Werewolves are doomed is the same regardless of whether they carry silver weapons or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}